+# ArbiLend — Security Audit Report
+
+**Scope:** `src/LendingMarket.sol`, `src/CollateralVault.sol`, `src/PriceOracle.sol`,
+`src/MarketProxy.sol`, `src/interfaces/*` (420 LoC total, commit `9852d3e`).
+**Target chain:** Arbitrum One. **Debt asset:** USDC. **Launch collateral:** wstETH.
+**Method:** manual review of the full source, cross-checked against the deployment
+parameters and collateral roadmap declared in `README.md`. No test suite exists, so
+nothing here is backed by an executing PoC — every finding is derived from the code path.
+
+---
+
+## Verdict
+
+**Do not deploy.** Four issues are individually sufficient to lose the entire book on day
+one, and three of them are one-line access-control omissions. Two of the four (C-1, C-2)
+give an anonymous caller full control of the protocol in a single transaction with no
+prerequisites. One (C-3) fires with no attacker at all — it liquidates honest users at
+199% collateralisation.
+
+The good news: the top of this list is cheap to fix. C-1 through C-4 are roughly a day of
+work plus tests. The High section is where the real engineering time goes.
+
+---
+
+## Ranked summary
+
+Hand rows 1–4 to the team Monday. Rows 5–13 before any real money moves. The rest before
+the collateral shortlist in the README gets listed.
+
+| # | Sev | Contract · function | One line |
+|---|-----|---------------------|----------|
+| C-1 | Critical | `LendingMarket.upgradeTo` | No access control — anyone upgrades the proxy and drains everything |
+| C-2 | Critical | `LendingMarket.setOracle` | No access control — anyone sets prices, mints debt or liquidates the book |
+| C-3 | Critical | `LendingMarket.healthFactor` | Divides before multiplying — positions at 199% LTV are liquidatable |
+| C-4 | Critical | `LendingMarket.setLiquidationThreshold` | No access control — force-liquidate every position for the 5% bonus |
+| H-1 | High | `PriceOracle.getPrice` | `latestAnswer()`, no staleness / negative / round checks |
+| H-2 | High | `PriceOracle` config (per README) | wstETH priced off a **stETH/USD** feed — ~20% collateral undervaluation |
+| H-3 | High | `PriceOracle.getPrice` | No Arbitrum L2 sequencer-uptime check — mass unfair liquidation after an outage |
+| H-4 | High | `LendingMarket.borrowWithSig` | No nonce, no deadline — signature replayable forever |
+| H-5 | High | `LendingMarket.borrow` / `liquidateAll` | `borrow(0)` appends to `borrowers` for free — permanent keeper DoS |
+| H-6 | High | `CollateralVault.withdraw` | Transfer before state update — reentrant drain once a hook token is listed |
+| H-7 | High | Both contracts, all ERC20 calls | Return values unchecked — USDT is on the shortlist |
+| H-8 | High | `LendingMarket._liquidate` | No close factor, liquidator overpays when underwater — bad debt sticks |
+| H-9 | High | `LendingMarket.accrueInterest` | Interest keyed to `block.number × 12s` on Arbitrum |
+| M-1 | Medium | `LendingMarket.initialize` | Front-runnable; implementation left uninitialised |
+| M-2 | Medium | `CollateralVault.deposit` | Credits `amount`, not amount received — breaks on fee-on-transfer and rebasing |
+| M-3 | Medium | `LendingMarket.listCollateral` | No feed check, no `decimals()` check, no delist path — bricks health checks |
+| M-4 | Medium | `LendingMarket.collateralValueUsd` | Unbounded token loop inside every health check |
+| M-5 | Medium | `LendingMarket.upgradeTo` | No `isContract` check — upgrade to an EOA freezes the protocol silently |
+| M-6 | Medium | `LendingMarket.setBorrowRate` etc. | No parameter bounds, no timelock, single-EOA owner |
+| M-7 | Medium | `LendingMarket.repay` | Transfer before state update (CEI) |
+| M-8 | Medium | Protocol-wide | No pause / emergency stop |
+| L-1 … L-10 | Low/Info | various | See below |
