+## C-3 — `healthFactor` divides before it multiplies, so healthy users get liquidated
+
+**Severity:** Critical · **Contract:** `LendingMarket` · **Function:** `healthFactor` (L146–151),
+reached from `liquidate`, `liquidateAll`, `_borrow`, `requireHealthy`
+
+```solidity
+return (collateralValueUsd(user) / debtUsd) * liquidationThreshold * WAD / BPS;
+```
+
+`collateralValueUsd` and `debtValueUsd` both return 1e18-scaled USD, so
+`collateralValueUsd(user) / debtUsd` is a **small integer** — it truncates the collateral
+ratio to a whole number before any of the scaling is applied. The 1e18 fixed-point precision
+this function claims in its own docstring is destroyed on the first operation.
+
+Worked numbers at the README's 8000 bps threshold, which nominally allows borrowing up to
+125% collateralisation:
+
+| Actual collateral ratio | `C/D` truncated | Health factor | Liquidatable? | Correct answer |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 1.24× | 1 | 0.8e18 | yes | yes |
+| 1.50× | 1 | 0.8e18 | **yes** | **no** |
+| 1.99× | 1 | 0.8e18 | **yes** | **no** |
+| 2.00× | 2 | 1.6e18 | no | no |
+| 2.99× | 2 | 1.6e18 | no | no |
+
+**What the unlucky user gets.** They deposit $199k of wstETH, borrow $100k of USDC — a
+conservative, doubly-overcollateralised position that any lending market on Arbitrum would
+call safe — and they are liquidatable the instant the transaction lands. A keeper running
+`liquidateAll()` repays their $100k debt and seizes $105k of their collateral. The user is
+down the 5% bonus and their position is force-closed, through no fault of their own and with
+no price movement required.
+
+Note the failure is *one-directional*: the truncation only ever rounds the health factor
+down, so the protocol never under-liquidates — it only ever over-liquidates. Every single
+error is paid for by a user. And the effect is worst for the most conservative borrowers,
+because it makes the effective requirement a hard 2.0× rather than the advertised 1.25×.
+
+`_borrow` runs the same check, so this also silently halves everyone's advertised borrowing
+power.
+
+**Fix.** Multiply first, divide once, at the end:
+
+```solidity
+function healthFactor(address user) public view returns (uint256) {
+    uint256 debtUsd = debtValueUsd(user);
+    if (debtUsd == 0) return type(uint256).max;
+    return collateralValueUsd(user) * liquidationThreshold * WAD / (BPS * debtUsd);
+}
+```
+
+Then add an invariant test asserting that a position at exactly
+`BPS * WAD / liquidationThreshold` collateralisation has `healthFactor == WAD`, and fuzz
+ratios across the boundary. The same "divide last" discipline should be applied to
+`collateralValueUsd` and `_liquidate`, which are correct today only because each of their
+individual divisions is by a token unit.
+
