+# High
+
+## H-1 — Oracle accepts unvalidated, deprecated Chainlink data
+
+**Severity:** High · **Contract:** `PriceOracle` · **Function:** `getPrice` (L39–45)
+
+```solidity
+int256 answer = feed.latestAnswer();
+return uint256(answer) * 10 ** (18 - feed.decimals());
+```
+
+Three separate defects in two lines:
+
+1. **`latestAnswer()` is deprecated.** It has no `updatedAt`, so there is no way to know the
+   answer is fresh. If an aggregator stops updating — node outage, feed deprecation, a fresh
+   feed that has never been written — this returns a stale or zero price indefinitely and the
+   market keeps trading against it. Chainlink's own docs tell integrators to use
+   `latestRoundData()`; the interface at `src/interfaces/IAggregatorV3.sol:11` already declares it.
+2. **No negative check.** `uint256(answer)` on a negative `int256` wraps to a value near
+   `2^256`. Multiplying that by `10 ** 10` overflows and reverts under 0.8.x checked
+   arithmetic, so a negative answer bricks every health check and every liquidation until the
+   feed recovers — a full protocol freeze at exactly the moment liquidations are needed.
+3. **No circuit-breaker awareness.** Chainlink aggregators clamp to `minAnswer`/`maxAnswer`.
+   During a violent depeg the feed reports the floor, not the market price. This is the exact
+   mechanism that cost Venus ~$11M in the LUNA collapse.
+
+**What the unlucky user gets.** A stale wstETH price during a fast move means either their
+healthy position is liquidated against a price that no longer exists, or an underwater
+position cannot be liquidated and the treasury eats the loss. On the USDC feed the same
+staleness reprices everyone's debt at once.
+
+**Fix.**
+
+```solidity
+function getPrice(address token) external view returns (uint256) {
+    IAggregatorV3 feed = feeds[token];
+    if (address(feed) == address(0)) revert FeedNotSet(token);
+
+    (uint80 roundId, int256 answer, , uint256 updatedAt, uint80 answeredInRound) = feed.latestRoundData();
+    if (answer <= 0) revert BadPrice(token);
+    if (updatedAt == 0 || answeredInRound < roundId) revert IncompleteRound(token);
+    if (block.timestamp - updatedAt > staleAfter[token]) revert StalePrice(token);
+
+    uint8 d = feed.decimals();
+    if (d > 18) revert UnsupportedFeedDecimals(token);
+    return uint256(answer) * 10 ** (18 - d);
+}
+```
+
+Set `staleAfter` per feed from that feed's published heartbeat plus a margin — do not use one
+global constant, the wstETH and USDC feeds have different heartbeats.
+
