+## H-4 — `borrowWithSig` signatures have no nonce and no deadline
+
+**Severity:** High · **Contract:** `LendingMarket` · **Function:** `borrowWithSig` (L162–168)
+
+```solidity
+bytes32 BORROW_TYPEHASH = keccak256("Borrow(address borrower,uint256 amount)");
+...
+if (ecrecover(digest, v, r, s) != borrower) revert BadSignature();
+_borrow(borrower, amount);
+```
+
+The signed struct contains only `(borrower, amount)`. There is no nonce, no deadline, no
+consumed-signature mapping.
+
+**What the attacker gets.**
+
+- **Unlimited replay.** A signature the borrower produced once — intending a single
+  $10k borrow — is a permanent, bearer instrument authorising a $10k borrow *every time the
+  borrower has the capacity for one*. Anyone who has ever seen it (it is in calldata on a
+  public chain forever) can resubmit it. Each replay pushes the borrower closer to
+  liquidation and adds interest they did not ask for. An attacker replays it repeatedly until
+  the position sits fractionally above `WAD`, then waits for the smallest adverse tick and
+  liquidates for the 5% bonus. The victim's only defence is to never leave borrowing capacity
+  unused.
+- **No expiry.** A signature issued during a quiet market is still valid a year later in a
+  crisis, at a completely different risk profile.
+- **`ecrecover` returns `address(0)` on malformed input.** The check is `!= borrower`, so a
+  garbage signature passed with `borrower == address(0)` reaches `_borrow(address(0), amount)`.
+  In practice USDC reverts on transfer to the zero address, so this stops there rather than
+  burning funds — but it is a missing guard, not a safe design, and it will not be safe for
+  every future debt asset.
+- **Malleability.** No EIP-2 `s`-range or `v ∈ {27,28}` check, so every signature has a twin.
+  Irrelevant while replay is unlimited anyway; relevant the moment you add a
+  used-signature mapping and forget the range check alongside it.
+
+**Fix.** Put a nonce and a deadline in the typehash, check both, and use OpenZeppelin's
+`ECDSA.recover` (which reverts on `address(0)` and rejects malleable `s`):
+
+```solidity
+bytes32 constant BORROW_TYPEHASH =
+    keccak256("Borrow(address borrower,uint256 amount,uint256 nonce,uint256 deadline)");
+
+function borrowWithSig(address borrower, uint256 amount, uint256 deadline, uint8 v, bytes32 r, bytes32 s) external {
+    if (block.timestamp > deadline) revert SignatureExpired();
+    bytes32 structHash = keccak256(abi.encode(BORROW_TYPEHASH, borrower, amount, nonces[borrower]++, deadline));
+    bytes32 digest = keccak256(abi.encodePacked("\x19\x01", domainSeparator, structHash));
+    if (ECDSA.recover(digest, v, r, s) != borrower) revert BadSignature();
+    _borrow(borrower, amount);
+}
+```
+
+Adding `nonces` is an append-only storage addition, which the README says is permitted.
+
